/*
 * wcc_quartz.c.stub — macOS host backend skeleton.
 *
 * STATUS: HONEST STUB. Every function fails loudly; nothing here
 * pretends to work. Not compiled on Linux (no Quartz SDK), not
 * compiled on macOS yet. Implement on the free macOS verify loop:
 *   buy-wubu-a-mac/research/01-github-actions-free-loop.md
 *
 * Implementation notes (from research/05):
 * - libwayland-server builds on macOS via epoll-shim (MacPorts); the
 *   protocol half of the compositor is unchanged.
 * - Prefer the C APIs (CoreGraphics/ApplicationServices) over ObjC
 *   where possible: osxcross compile-checks from Linux stay useful,
 *   and the C surface is stable across macOS versions.
 * - Buffer import: the guest hands us BGRA shm (0x00RRGGBB in memory =
 *   B,G,R,00). CVPixelBufferCreateWithBytes or CGImageCreate with
 *   kCGImageAlphaNoneSkipLast; NO blending (the unused alpha byte must
 *   not composite the desktop transparent — same rule as the GLX path).
 * - Frame pacing: CVDisplayLink; present-on-change memcmp against a
 *   compositor-owned last copy (the XShm/GLX rule, unchanged).
 * - Input: CGEventTapCreate for mouse/keyboard; translate to the seat
 *   paths. Keyboard focus rules differ from XGrabKeyboard — read the
 *   macOS event-tap docs before wiring, don't guess.
 */

